# Review test for M9's failure path (user/root/src/net.rs; docs/design.md,
# "Failures" under "Networking"): a virtio-net fault ends the run with
# failure through watch, whatever root waits on. Root starts everything
# as test=net does, then reads a line as client 1, which has focus; the
# harness types Enter once net has pinged the gateway, after which no
# server prints again. Root prints its line and syncs, suspends
# virtio-net, writes its rip 0 and resumes it, and calls its Stats.
# virtio-net's next instruction fetch, at address 0, which nothing maps,
# is a VMFault (ip 0, address 0, a fetch, fsr 0x14: a user-mode fetch of
# a page not present); the kernel sends it on F with badge 4, and watch
# writes TEST FAIL naming virtio-net through Polled, and ends the run with
# DebugHalt(1). The next: lines show that nothing comes between root's
# line, watch's and the halt's two lines: root, in its call to the dead
# driver, prints nothing more, and net, which no frame reaches now,
# prints nothing either.
cmdline: test=virtio_net_fault
exit: failure
nic: virtio-net
expect: root: cmdline "test=virtio_net_fault"
expect: servers: virtio-net (priority 140, MSI-X IRQ
expect: virtio-net: up: MAC 52:54:00:12:34:56
expect: net: up: 10.0.2.15/24 via 10.0.2.2, MAC 52:54:00:12:34:56
expect: net: ping 10.0.2.2: reply 1, 56 bytes
send: \r                           # Enter: root's line
expect: virtio_net_fault: suspending virtio-net, setting its rip to 0 and resuming it
next: TEST FAIL: virtio-net fault 5 (VMFault), MR0 to MR3 0x0 0x0 0x1 0x14
next: dispatch: invocations preempted and restarted:   # DebugHalt's first line
next: DEBUG HALT 1 from TCB
forbid: virtio-net answered Stats after its rip was set to 0
forbid: watch did not end the run
forbid: TEST PASS
forbid: KERNEL PANIC
